    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d598">

                <pb facs="0702" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg606"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sternburg to Mr.
                            Day.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >German Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-07-07"><hi rendition="#italic">July 7,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: Acting under instructions of his
                    Government I am directed by his excellency the German ambassador to inquire
                    whether your Government are disposed to concur in the recommendation of the
                    Imperial German Government that all the chiefs living in exile with Mataafa
                    should not be permitted to return to Samoa on condition of their signing a
                    similar protocol to that to be signed by Mataafa regarding their loyalty toward
                    the Samoan government.</p>
                <p>Sir Julian Pauncefote informed me that he would telegraph to his Government as
                    soon as an agreement had been reached on this question between the Government of
                    the United States and the Imperial German Government.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. S. Sternburg.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
